    {
      "id": "CARD-AM-07-concept",
      "conceptId": "C-AM-07",
      "kind": "concept",
      "title": {
        "en": "Lowpass filtering and waveform comparison",
        "or": "Lowpass filtering ଓ Waveform ତୁଳନା"
      },
      "body": {
        "en": "A lowpass filter is the separation stage after product detection. Its useful passband must include the message frequencies while its attenuation rejects the components near twice the carrier. Our bounded model uses a 100 Hz message, a 2000 Hz carrier and a second-order Butterworth lowpass with 500 Hz cutoff. In a continuous Transfer Fcn block, H(s)=wc^2/(s^2+sqrt(2)*wc*s+wc^2), where wc=2*pi*500 rad/s. This filter does not remove every unwanted component perfectly. It introduces a startup transient and frequency-dependent phase lag. Compare the recovered signal after startup, checking frequency and amplitude while allowing the predicted phase shift rather than demanding an identical trace.",
        "or": "Product detection ପରେ Lowpass filter message frequency କୁ ରଖେ ଏବଂ ପ୍ରାୟ ଦୁଇଗୁଣ Carrier frequency ନିକଟର ଅଂଶ କମାଏ। ଆମ model ରେ Message 100 Hz, Carrier 2000 Hz ଓ second-order Butterworth filter ର Cutoff frequency 500 Hz। wc=2*pi*500 rad/s ଏବଂ H(s)=wc^2/(s^2+sqrt(2)*wc*s+wc^2)। ଏହା ସମସ୍ତ unwanted component ସମ୍ପୂର୍ଣ୍ଣ ହଟାଏ ନାହିଁ। ଆରମ୍ଭରେ transient ଏବଂ ପରେ Phase lag ଥାଏ। Startup ପରେ output ତୁଳନା କରନ୍ତୁ। Frequency ଓ Amplitude ଯାଞ୍ଚ କରିବା ସହିତ Filter ର Phase lag କୁ ଧ୍ୟାନରେ ରଖନ୍ତୁ।"
      },
